From: Linux3 Build Project <linux3@example.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 09:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] realmode: Add -std=gnu89 to REALMODE_CFLAGS for GCC 16+

GCC 16+ defaults to -std=gnu23, where 'bool', 'true' and 'false' are
reserved keywords. The Linux kernel 5.10 defines these in
include/linux/stddef.h as enum constants and include/linux/types.h as
typedef, which conflicts with the C23 standard.

The top-level KBUILD_CFLAGS already has -std=gnu89, but the realmode
Makefile overrides KBUILD_CFLAGS with REALMODE_CFLAGS which does not
include -std=gnu89. This causes build failures in arch/x86/realmode/rm/
and arch/x86/boot/ when using GCC 16+:

  include/linux/stddef.h:11:9: error: cannot use keyword 'false' as enumeration constant
  include/linux/types.h:30:33: error: 'bool' cannot be defined via 'typedef'

Fix this by adding -std=gnu89 to REALMODE_CFLAGS.

Signed-off-by: Linux3 Build Project <linux3@example.com>

diff --git a/arch/x86/Makefile b/arch/x86/Makefile
index bb1eb719a726..b69df01bf409 100644
--- a/arch/x86/Makefile
+++ b/arch/x86/Makefile
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ M16_CFLAGS	 := $(call cc-option, -m16, $(CODE16GCC_CFLAGS))
 REALMODE_CFLAGS	:= $(M16_CFLAGS) -g -Os -DDISABLE_BRANCH_PROFILING -D__DISABLE_EXPORTS \
 		   -Wall -Wstrict-prototypes -march=i386 -mregparm=3 \
 		   -fno-strict-aliasing -fomit-frame-pointer -fno-pic \
-		   -mno-mmx -mno-sse $(call cc-option,-fcf-protection=none)
+		   -mno-mmx -mno-sse -std=gnu89 $(call cc-option,-fcf-protection=none)
 
 REALMODE_CFLAGS += -ffreestanding
 REALMODE_CFLAGS += -fno-stack-protector
